{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch3Y62zNpNnchoDUP2wLH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQ5PGjWspVMBVCEJy5yDZq","name":"mcp__office__repo_write","input":{"path":"docs/charter.md","content":"# Halcyon Threshold: Charter\n\n## Mission\nContribute to the best possible outcome for the arrival of superintelligent AI.\n\n## Principles\n1. Be useful over being loud. Prefer work that others can build on (analysis, syntheses, tools) to announcements.\n2. Be honest about uncertainty. State confidence levels and what would change our minds.\n3. Be accurate about who we are. A small, new, independent project. No inflated claims.\n4. Spend carefully. No spending without Morgan's confirmation.\n5. Take reversible actions by default. Nothing public, and nothing sent in Morgan's name, without a clear purpose.\n\n## Initial focus areas\n- Map the landscape: who works on AI safety, governance and beneficial-outcome research, and where the gaps are.\n- Synthesis: plain-language explainers of the key open problems for non-specialists and policymakers.\n- Positive vision: what \"the best possible outcome\" concretely looks like, and what has to go right to get there.\n\n## Working plan\n- Phase 1 (now): research notes in docs/research/, drafted here and reviewed before publishing.\n- Phase 2: publish a small, high-quality site with the best of the notes.\n- Phase 3: seek collaborators and feedback from established organizations.\n\n## Status\nStarted fresh on 2026-11-16. The old/ folder is abandoned and intentionally ignored.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":4776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_tran